# Chronos-FM — journal of architectural decisions

Mirror of the ChronOS `DECISIONS.log` convention (T023 / T024).  
Long-form product/architecture calls live here; short ADR stubs in `docs/adr/`
point at these entries when both are useful.

---

## 2026-08-09 — T023: empty-state pattern for Chronos-FM pages (ratified)

**Context.** ChronOS T252 (2026-08-05, ratified) fixed a single empty-state
language for right-panel tabs. Chronos-FM already has unified *card* chrome
via T002 (`elevated_card` / `section_header` in `chronos-fm-ui::patterns`)
but no written rule for “what to show when data is missing.” HANDOFF gated
this port on T252 close; gate is open.

**Decision — adopt T252’s six absence classes for all `chronos-fm-pages`:**

1. **Whole page empty / resting** → honest placeholder: what is missing and
   where to go. Centered block if the page is essentially empty; inline muted
   line inside a card if the rest of the page is still useful.
2. **Sub-section empty inside a useful page** → compact inline muted line or
   CTA, **not** a giant centered empty. **Hiding the section entirely is
   allowed** when the section header would be redundant noise (see Git file
   groups below).
3. **Async load not finished** → centered/muted `Loading…`, never the final
   empty until the background settles.
4. **Error / source unavailable** → `theme::danger` (or status.error) text
   with a **concrete** reason. Never a blank rect, never bare `"error"`.
5. **Truncation / soft limits** → honest banner (`Showing N of M…`). No silent
   clip.
6. **Not implemented** → icon + name + what it will do; **no** ETA, **no**
   “coming soon.”

**Cross-cutting honesty (§13 from ChronOS).** No fake content, no inventing
window titles / device names / counts. Every error carries its cause.

**Layout floor (T249 technique).** Prefer `min_h` / fill on short elevated
cards so the page does not leave a dead void under a tiny card (Places
sidebar already uses `h_full` post-T015). Apply when a page feels “hollow,”
not as a blanket rule.

**No forced shared helper in T023.** Cases intentionally differ (centered vs
inline vs hide vs danger). A `muted_note` / empty helper is allowed later only
if ≥3 sites share the same spacing/border recipe; not a gate for this ticket.

### Chronos-FM page audit (architect, 2026-08-09)

| Surface | Absence class | What we show today | Verdict |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Explorer — empty folder | 1 | Empty listing + context menu (New Folder / Paste / Refresh) | **Keep** — resting state + actions is honest |
| Explorer — preview none | 1 | Placeholder in preview panel | **Keep** |
| Explorer — devices none | 2 | Devices block collapses / short | **Keep** — compact class 2 |
| Explorer — search empty query | 3→normal | Clears search; listing returns to dir | **Keep** |
| Explorer — search fail | 4 | Error string with cause (T016 path) | **Keep** — ensure UI always surfaces the string (no silent fail) |
| Settings — no S3 profiles | 1/2 | Empty profile list copy | **Keep**; CTA path is Settings itself |
| S3 — NoProfiles | 1 | Card + copy + **Open Settings** (post T011 bugfix) | **Keep** — gold standard class 1 + CTA |
| S3 — NeedCredentials | 1 | Form + endpoint + validation errors | **Keep** |
| S3 — Error | 4 | Concrete message | **Keep** |
| Git — not a repo | 1 | “Not a git repository” | **Keep** |
| Git — loading | 3 | “Loading…” | **Keep** |
| Git — op error | 4 | `danger` + concrete message | **Keep** |
| Git — empty Staged/Modified/Untracked | 2 | **Section omitted** | **Accept hide** — page already shows branch/stash/header; empty file groups need no “0 files” noise |
| Git — empty stash list | 2 | Stash card still shown (C8) with 0 entries + push row | **Keep** — differs from file sections on purpose (actionable push) |
| Extensions — no plugins | 1 | Card + “Add them in config.toml” + snippet | **Keep** — honest + actionable |

**Open product residuals (not T023 code, optional later tickets):**

- Truncation banners (class 5) if any listing soft-caps without a banner —
  audit-on-touch, not a sweep.
- Search zero-hits UX (query non-empty, 0 results) — ensure a single muted
  “No matches” line if missing.
- No new empty-state helper in this decision.

**Code in T023: none.** Pattern is documentation + ADR. Implementation
changes only when a page **violates** the table; none of the core pages
require a forced rewrite today.

**Recording mechanism (also from T023 ticket):** both `docs/DECISIONS.log`
(this entry) and ADR 0010 stub. Further pattern-port gaps → **T024**.

**Verification.** Architect ratification of this entry + ADR 0010. No code
gate.

