## 2026-08-09 — T024: pattern-port remainder decisions (ratified)

**Context.** T023 closed empty-state + DECISIONS.log mechanism. T024
addresses the remaining ~40% of ChronOS pattern-port gaps: rejected/
directory, notes/ directory, MIGRATION.md artifact, and per-project
skills. Architect ratification 2026-08-09 via T024.

### Decision 1 — `rejected/` directory: PORTED

Create `docs/orchestration/tasks/rejected/` mirroring ChronOS convention.
Rules:
- REFUTED/REJECTED reports move to `rejected/` (physical move or
  duplicate with reference)
- Superseded tickets (suffix `-superseded-by-Txxx.md`) go there too
- The original report in `report/` keeps its errata block — `rejected/`
  is the final resting place, not a replacement for the errata
- Filename convention: suffix `-REJECTED.md` or `-superseded-by-Txxx.md`

First inhabitant: `T011-s3-tab-live-report.md` (REFUTED with errata).

### Decision 2 — `notes/` directory: NOT PORTED

`docs/orchestration/tasks/notes/` is not created. Session-knowledge is
covered by `.workbuddy/memory/` (MEMORY.md + dated files). ChronOS
`notes/` was ad-hoc; `.workbuddy/memory/` is the deliberate replacement.
No duplication needed.

### Decision 3 — `MIGRATION.md`: NOT PORTED

`docs/orchestration/tasks/MIGRATION.md` from ChronOS is a historical
artifact of the per-agent → per-task migration (2026-07-22). Chronos-FM
started with per-task accounting from day one — no migration document
is applicable. Explicitly recorded so the question does not resurface.

### Decision 4 — per-project skills: ON DEMAND

ChronOS has 11 skills not ported to FM. Rule: port a skill only when
an FM task requires it. No bulk import. Likely first candidates:
`tokio-coop-budget-on-main-thread`, `rtl-text-rendering` — both
relevant to a gpui project with tokio in services. Each port includes
adaptation to FM paths and conventions.

