### Decision — Source fix: T014-A frame layout memo silently dropped text (T043 real root cause)

**Date:** 2026-08-10
**Ticket:** T043 (blocks T037 §7 Places), also the true root cause behind
T037's "sparse list" / missing header/breadcrumb text symptoms.

**Context.** T043's report ("FIX-ACCEPT", self-closed, no architect verdict)
claimed the Places-empty bug was `h_resizable` not allocating sidebar space,
fixed by bypassing `resizable_panel()` with a fixed-width `div()`. That bypass
is real and harmless, but a fresh release-binary + live grim (this session,
`chronos-fm --theme dark`, settle 8-15s) showed the sidebar panel painting
with **icons only — zero text**, including the "Places" section header
itself, matching T037's earlier "no Places content" / "sparse list" reports.
The claimed "81,979 FG text pixels" evidence in the T043 report does not
match live behavior and was not reproducible.

**Root cause (Claim → Evidence).** `Source/gpui/src/taffy.rs`'s T014-A
frame-level layout memo (`TaffyLayoutEngine::compute_layout`) skips
`taffy.compute_layout_with_measure` entirely whenever this frame's layout
fingerprint (styles + child counts + content keys, in request order) matches
the previous frame's. `request_layout`/`request_measured_layout_with_content_key`
rebuild the full element tree — including a brand-new `TextLayout`
(`Rc<RefCell<None>>`, `Source/gpui/src/elements/text.rs`) — every single
render, regardless of whether the memo later skips computing. When it skips,
that frame's freshly-built `TextLayout` never gets its `measure` closure
invoked, so `TextLayoutInner` (glyph shaping, size) is never populated.
T035 (2026-08-09, ACCEPTed) turned the resulting `unwrap()` panic in
`TextLayout::prepaint`/`paint` into a silent early-return — correct for
genuinely un-laid-out zero-size elements, but it also **masked** this memo
bug: instead of crashing, affected text simply stops painting, with no log,
no test coverage, no visible signal. Any UI whose layout tree repeats
identically frame-to-frame (i.e. most idle UI, not just Chronos-FM) loses
its text after the first "memo hit" frame. Confirmed by disabling the memo
fast path and observing Places labels ("Home", "Desktop", …), the "Places"
header, and toolbar/breadcrumb text all reappear on a fresh release grim.

**Fix (Source, `taffy.rs`).** Added `frame_has_measured_leaf: bool`, set by
`request_measured_layout_with_content_key` (covers `request_measured_layout`
too) and reset in `clear()`. The T014-A fast path in `compute_layout` now
requires `!self.frame_has_measured_leaf` in addition to the existing
fingerprint/available-space match, so any frame containing a measured leaf
(text, or any future custom `request_measured_layout*` element) always runs
the real `compute_layout_with_measure` pass. Pure box-layout frames (no text)
still get the memo's perf win. Two new unit tests
(`measured_leaf_disables_frame_memo_fast_path`,
`plain_layout_leaves_memo_fast_path_eligible`) plus the three existing
T014-A tests pass (`cargo test -p gpui --lib taffy`, 6/6 green).

**Verification.** `cargo build --release -p chronos-fm` clean; live grim
(`script/dev/t037_smoke.sh`, 15s settle, real `hyprctl`-verified
`class=chronos-fm` window) shows: "Places" header + "quick access" subtitle,
all seven place labels (Home/Desktop/Documents/Downloads/Music/Pictures/
Videos), two device rows (VTOYEFI, Ventoy), toolbar breadcrumb path text,
"40 Items" count, List/Grid toggle labels — all rendering correctly. Evidence
screenshot reviewed directly (vision), not programmatic pixel-only analysis.

**Residual (new, not this fix).** Same grim shows the Grid content pane
**empty** despite "40 Items" in the breadcrumb — `filtered_entries` is
apparently not reaching `grid::render` even though `ensure_loaded`/`reload`/
`apply_filter` run synchronously before it in the same render pass. This is
a distinct defect (listing-state plumbing, not text painting) — filed as
**T044** rather than folded into T043's text-rendering fix.

**Why this belongs in Source, not Chronos-FM.** The bug is in the shared
GPUI fork's layout engine and can affect any consumer (ChronOS shell
included) whose render tree repeats between frames — not specific to
Chronos-FM's sidebar. Fixing it in Chronos-FM would mean avoiding
memo-triggering render patterns app-wide, which is not tractable.


### Decision — T045 root cause: snapshot_memo poisons uncomputed siblings

**Date:** 2026-08-10  
**Finding:** Nested `v_virtual_list::measure_item` → `compute_layout` miss path
calls `snapshot_memo`, which walks **global** `frame_node_order` and caches
`layout_bounds` for nodes not yet computed this frame as `(0,0)/(0,0)`.
Poisons sidebar/toolbar SVG/text absolute bounds for the rest of the frame.
**Repro:** `Source/gpui-component/examples/t045_repro` (isolated).  
**Fix direction:** scope `snapshot_memo` to the subtree of the compute root
(or skip nested snapshots / do not cache uncomputed layouts).  
**Status:** RC accepted; fix not shipped. Blocks T037.


### Decision — T045 fix shipped (snapshot_memo subtree scope)

**Date:** 2026-08-10  
**Change:** Source `gpui/src/taffy.rs` — `snapshot_memo(root, space)` only
layout_bounds nodes in `subtree_ids(root)`.  
**Verification:** gpui taffy 8/8 tests; live grim Places+listing; 0 zero-size errors.  
**Status:** ACCEPT. Unblocks T037.

